@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - Watch and completion loops are command instructions

rectangle "Host runtime / local scheduler\nstarts a requested command" as host
rectangle "desk-watch\nread baseline before refresh" as watch
rectangle "Refresh chain, Greeks and exposure\ncompare same underlying / expiry" as refresh
rectangle "Material change or unavailable input?\nspot, IV, regime, walls, RR, degradation" as change
rectangle "Report changes with prior values\nor no material change; stop" as report
rectangle "desk-complete\nread six criteria from artifacts" as complete
rectangle "Run only missing / failing stages\nchoose expiry, widen band or raise draws" as work
rectangle "Stop\nall criteria met, structural blocker\nor configured attempt limit" as stop
host --> watch
watch --> refresh
refresh --> change
change --> report
host --> complete
complete --> work : unmet and repairable
work --> complete : re-check
complete --> stop
note bottom of watch
Observation only. This command does not open,
mark or close a paper or real position.
Unavailable values are not numeric changes.
end note
note bottom of complete
Six criteria: IV coverage, ladder size, walls/smile,
rankable plans, converged horizon, degradation reasons.
These are prompt instructions, not the LangGraph evaluator.
The host supplies recurrence and attempt limits.
end note

caption Sources: .claude/commands/desk-watch.md and desk-complete.md. Commands depend on the host runtime for scheduling.
@enduml
